            <h3 class="cs-font_24 mt-4 mb-2">Do we have enough traffic for A/B testing?</h3>
            <p>Honestly, many sites don't. A valid A/B test needs enough conversions per variant to separate signal from noise, and low-traffic sites can wait months for an answer the math still can't defend. Where that's you, we say so and use sequential measurement instead: fix the obvious problems, measure before vs after over comparable periods, and accept slightly less certainty in exchange for actually moving.</p>
